      "writtenOn": "2019-05-22T20:38:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The likelihood of two events logged at the same second is extremely low, OTOH the timestamp is used when iterating through the saved log, this is why it is important that entries have different timestamps.\n\nI feel that this compromise (risking an incorrect timestamp) is acceptable, since the events are supposed to be happening very seldom, seeing two events in the log one second apart would be a hint that the second (and  the following immediate events) could be logged at a time few seconds off.",
      "parentUuid": "109d24b8_56d78a09",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 70,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 35
      },
